WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:08.050
Let's go to the news conference
&gt;&gt; You see several subject matter experts

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:12.790
from the unified command who introduced themselves
momentarily.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.270
These individuals represent only a small fraction
of the many dedicated professionals working

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:21.460
around the clock on this complex response
effort.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.230
We understand this is an extremely difficult
time for the families of the missing crew

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:31.140
members aboard the titan and our thoughts
go out to them and the crew.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:36.170
The unified command team is working tirelessly
to bring all available assets and expertise

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:41.630
to bear as quickly as possible in response
to this complex operation.

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:45.989
We remain in close contact go with the family
members and the crew to ensure they're fully

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:50.260
aware of our current and future search efforts.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.520
Additionally, we've made close contact with
the British and

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.520
[1:02:14 PM]

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.649
contact with the British and French consulates
general to make sure they're fully apriced

00:00:57.649 --> 00:01:01.480
of our efforts.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.479
We're incredibly grateful for the full spectrum
of international assistance that has been

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:11.520
provided including an expert sub mariner from
the royal Navy who is here with us serving

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.229
aboard as a critical member of our team.

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:23.369
Additionally, a team of highly fif teams are
en route to aid in the search more over, our

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:29.759
Canadian partners have been providing critical
leadership and significant response capabilities

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:32.579
since the beginning of our efforts.

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:38.560
Again, this is an incredibly complex search
operation requiring surface and subsurface

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.560
elements.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.990
And our unified approach is critical.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:48.080
The location of the search, 900 miles east
of cape cod and 400 miles southeast of St.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:52.020
John's makes very difficult to mobilize large
amounts of equipment

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.020
[1:03:16 PM]

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.750
large amounts of equipment quickly.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:02:03.070
We've been able to provide air and surface
search assets to search below the surface.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:08.660
We currently have five service assets searching
for the "Titan" and we expect ten to surface

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:11.330
in the next few hours.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:18.260
There are two rovs actively sxeching two more
are en route.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:23.660
We've received incredible support with aviation
assets from our coast guard air station in

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:30.080
Elizabeth city, the air National Guard and
Canadian armed forces.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.879
Today there are two back to back p-3 flights.

00:02:32.879 --> 00:02:41.920
One is ongoing now totaling 14 hours of continuous
onscene coverage and two c-130 coverage all

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.680
throughout the day and into the evening.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.409
Yesterday the Canadian p-3 detected underwater
noises in the search area.

00:02:49.409 --> 00:02:53.870
As a result, rov operations were relocated
in an attempt to explore the origin of the

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:54.870
noises.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:55.870
[1:04:16 PM]

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:56.870
noises.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.990
Although the rov has not gotten results, they
continue.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:07.280
Additionally it has been shared with our U.S.
Navy experts for further analysis which will

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.760
be considered in future search plans.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:15.660
The surface search is now approximately two
times the size of Connecticut and it is up

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.200
to two and a half miles deep.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.810
Exponentially expanding the size of the search
area.

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:27.230
We have to factor in ever changing weather
conditions, currents and sea states that expand

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.480
the the search area every hour.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:35.379
There is an enormous complexity with this
case due to it being so far offshore and the

00:03:35.379 --> 00:03:38.860
coordination between multiple agencies and
nations.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:43.459
We greatly appreciate the outpouring of support
and offers to provide additional equipment.

00:03:43.459 --> 00:03:48.230
The unified command continues to prioritize
assets and resources in order to provide the

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:51.740
best capability in the most timely manner.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:56.079
This includes weighing multiple factors to
identify the most effective resources available

00:03:56.079 --> 00:03:57.620
to the response operation.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:58.620
[1:05:18 PM]

00:03:58.620 --> 00:03:59.620
the response operation.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:03.790
With careful consideration to timeliness of
equipment arriving on scene, usefulness and

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:07.540
ability to deliver assets to the search area.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:12.640
Over the past 48 hours, we have through incredible
unit of effort mobilized and implemented a

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.050
tremendous amount of expertise.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:20.190
In addition to the ships and aircraft previously
mentioned we've dispatched two subject matter

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:22.019
experts.

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:29.100
They will serve as search coordinators on
scene for underwater operations.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.870
So I've been stressing unity of effort a lot
in this statement and that's because it is

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:37.009
absolutely critical to this complex operation.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:41.220
Again, our thoughts and prayer are with the
crew of the "Titan" and their loved ones.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:45.759
We will work as hard and quickly as possible
in an effort to locate them.

00:04:45.759 --> 00:04:47.630
I will take a few questions.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:52.600
Before I do that, I'm going to have each of
the members, the team, introduce themselves

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.880
and I'll take some questions.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.419
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon.

00:04:56.419 --> 00:04:57.960
[1:06:19 PM]

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.509
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon.

00:04:59.509 --> 00:05:00.910
I'm Paul Hankins.

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:08.190
I'm the director for salvage operations with
the U.S. Navy's supervisor of salvage.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:16.330
&gt;&gt; Hello, I'm Carl from the oceanographic
institute.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:22.080
&gt;&gt; I'm an exchange officer currently serving
on the staff at Norfolk, Virginia.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.169
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon.

00:05:23.169 --> 00:05:32.880
Lieutenant commander Christie butler working
closely with Frederick.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:49.070
[ Inaudible question ]
&gt;&gt; So a couple thing.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:52.240
When you're in the middle of a search and
rescue, you always have hope.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.800
That's why we do what we do.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.620
With respect to the noises, we don't know
what they are to be

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:58.620
[1:07:20 PM]

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.830
don't know what they are to be frank with
you.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.570
The p-3 detected noises.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:04.490
That's why they're doing what they're doing.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:09.090
That's why they put sonar in the water.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:12.520
What I can tell you is we're searching in
the area where the noises were detected and

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.120
we'll continue to do so.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:18.770
And we hope that when we're able to get additional
rovs which will get there in the morning,

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:23.259
the intent will be to search in those areas
where the noises were detected.

00:06:23.259 --> 00:06:28.840
If they continue to be detected, and then
put additional rovs where the search was originally

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:35.060
taking place.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:36.720
I hadn't heard 30-minute intervals.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.150
Here's what I can tell you.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:43.830
So I am not a trained ear for underwater aquatics.

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:46.400
That's why we have a team of experts analyzing
that data.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:52.050
It was sent immediately to the Navy last night
and it was analyzed overnight.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.050
They're still looking at it.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.050
Inconclusive.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:55.060
I think the important pieces.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.009
We're searching in the area

00:06:57.009 --> 00:06:58.009
[1:08:20 PM]

00:06:58.009 --> 00:06:59.830
We're searching in the area where the noises
were detected.

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:05.349
&gt;&gt; Can you talk about the time line?

00:07:05.349 --> 00:07:09.900
&gt;&gt; A time line in what respect?

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.639
Oh, okay.

00:07:12.639 --> 00:07:16.970
So in terms of, we talked about the action
number.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.460
I think there's an important point.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:22.370
The oxygen, that's just one piece of data.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.370
Right?

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:25.960
There are a lot of pieces of data that we
need to consider.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:31.810
And we're continuously looking at that and
we're continuously doing that throughout the

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:32.810
search.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:35.960
But that's not the only thing that is important.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:39.580
Right now our efforts are solely focused on
the search.

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:42.379
That is certainly a dialogue happening.

00:07:42.379 --> 00:07:44.290
But we're focused on searching at this point.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:47.180
&gt;&gt; Is this a recovery or a rescue?

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:49.190
&gt;&gt; A search and rescue 100%.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:53.560
We're smack dab in the middle of a search
and rescue and we'll continue to put every

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:58.240
asset we have to find the "Titan" and the
crew members.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:07:59.630
[1:09:21 PM]

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.009
crew members.

00:08:01.009 --> 00:08:08.639
&gt;&gt; Can you confirm some sort of rectangular
object has been spotted?

00:08:08.639 --> 00:08:12.260
There was some sort of report about that.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:13.260
&gt;&gt; So a couple things.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.060
The rovs, each one brings different capability.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:17.409
The rovs diving today, what is the depth?

00:08:17.409 --> 00:08:18.490
Yep, 4,000 meters.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:23.130
And additional rovs arriving tomorrow have
additional depth capability.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:28.630
With respect to an object, so yesterday, one
of the aircraft did see an object.

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:30.190
I will tell you this.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:33.269
In search and rescue missions when aircraft
are flying continuously, there is stuff out

00:08:33.269 --> 00:08:35.740
in the ocean that is floating.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.690
We went back and looked at it.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:40.120
We didn't determine it to be debris.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:45.710
We don't think it correlates with the case
and it is not uncommon at all during an active

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:46.710
search.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:47.710
You see things and then you go look at them.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:48.710
&gt;&gt; When were these noises first heard?

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:52.990
Do you have any information in terms of food
and water that the

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:55.890
[1:10:21 PM]

00:08:55.890 --> 00:09:05.700
terms of food and water that the men might
have on board?

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:13.380
&gt;&gt; So several p-3 flights have heard the noises
yesterday and we put assets there.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:15.399
We relocated assets immediately.

00:09:15.399 --> 00:09:19.440
With respect to food and water, it is my understanding
there are limited rations.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:24.450
I can't tell you exactly how much they have
aboard but they do have some limited rations

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.740
aboard.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:35.000
[ Inaudible question ]
&gt;&gt; I think you need to be careful.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.100
We need to have hope, right?

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:39.380
But I can't tell you what the noises are.

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:42.290
What I can tell you, and I think this is the
most important point.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:46.860
We're searching where the noises are and that's
all we can do at this point.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.690
&gt;&gt; -- Right now about the status?

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:54.460
Are the noises continuing now?

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:59.000
&gt;&gt; So I just, it is my understanding the p-3
heard noises today as well.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.243
I want to take an opportunity to invite Carl
to the podium to

00:10:01.243 --> 00:10:02.243
[1:11:23 PM]

00:10:02.243 --> 00:10:08.120
invite Carl to the podium to talk a little
bit about, he has more expertise in underwater

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:12.589
acoustics and complain to speak to that in
general.

00:10:12.589 --> 00:10:21.190
There are noises below the surface of the
ocean.

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:30.420
&gt;&gt; Again, from the oceanographic institution.

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:33.220
The association a very complex place.

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:39.260
Obviously human sounds, nature sounds, and
it is very difficult to discern what the source

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:41.200
of the noises are at times.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:44.470
I can tell that you this team has multiple
sensors.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:46.340
They're in the area.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:52.160
They're sending data back expeditiously to
the best in the world people to analyze that

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:57.620
data and then they're feeding the results
bag to the unified team and they're making

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:59.700
decisions.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.160
So we're here in an advisory

